nt with checked fixed-width arithmetic; usize/isize assume 64 bits","assumptions":["Rust integer arithmetic uses checked overflow behavior (debug/test profile); release wrapping arithmetic is outside this draft contract","String case conversion depends on the source and host Unicode tables","Concrete admitted constants require bounded checked evaluation with original parser source links; const fn runtime eligibility alone proves no all-input compile-time behavior","Immutable strings encode scalar values; monomorphic tagged values encode Option/Result; vectors/slices are immutable arrays"],"observation":"checked value results, local scalar mutation, immutable constructors, lazy future polling and named host effects; carried items supply no executable behavior"},"counts":{"executable":4,"executableFunctions":1,"executableConstants":3,"executableTypes":0,"executableConstructors":0,"carried":6,"preserved":11},"items":[{"term":"trivia","name":null,"span":{"start":0,"end":1203,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":0,"byteEnd":1209},"sha256":"a85c2e32f73959fd1984b3737fff94c0a209e1f4c4effb03918e89f10ac743c6","source":"//! The stand-in used when a command will never sign anything.\n//!\n//! Several commands act on another deployment, or only read local files, and\n//! so have no use for this machine's signing secret. Rather than thread an\n//! `Option` through every construction site, they install a stand-in — and the\n//! stand-in was an ordinary string, which meant a command that turned out to\n//! run *locally* after all went on to sign real tokens and encrypt real vendor\n//! API keys with a value published in the source (issue #300).\n//!\n//! Two things fix that. The value now begins with a NUL byte, which no\n//! environment variable or command line can carry, so it cannot be supplied\n//! deliberately or arrived at by accident. And every place that actually uses\n//! the secret — signing, validating, encrypting — refuses it, so the sentinel\n//! is inert rather than merely unlikely: reaching a signer with it produces\n//! the ordinary `TOKEN_SECRET is required` error, before anything is written.\n\n/// Marks a secret that exists only to satisfy a type, and must never be used.\n///\n/// The NUL prefix is what makes it unforgeable: `std::env::var` cannot return\n/// a value containing one, and neither can argv.\n","status":"preserved","diagnostic":null,"comment":true},{"term":"const","name":"SENTINEL","span":{"start":1203,"end":1272,"unit":"utf16","byteStart":1209,"byteEnd":1278},"sha256":"577becb0b3ae886cf4aad3cdeac727d476234e5df0c0619d4a4543cd5402a14b","source":"const SENTINEL: &str = \"\\u{0}link-assistant-router:no-token-secret:\";","status":"executable","diagnostic":null,"comment":false,"configuration":{"status":"active","attributes":[],"diagnostics":[]},"semantic":{"checkedIR":{"k":"fn","name":"rp_746f6b656e5f7365637265742e53454e54494e454c","params":[],"ret":{"kind":"string","rustSourceType":true,"rustOwnership":{"kind":"borrowed","source":"str"},"rustBorrowLifetime":{"kind":"elided","source":"borrowed-str-type","span":{"start":4035909,"end":4035913},"tokens":[{"kind":"punct","value":"&","span":{"start":4035909,"end":4035910}},{"kind":"identifier","value":"str","span":{"start":4035910,"end":4035913}}]}},"body":{"k":"lit","type":{"kind":"string","rustOwnership":{"kind":"borrowed","source":"str"},"rustBorrowLifetime":{"kind":"static","source":"string-literal","span":{"start":4035916,"end":4035961}}},"value":"\u0000link-assistant-router:no-token-secret:","span":{"start":4035916,"end":4035961}},"constant":true,"span":{"start":4035893,"end":4035898},"fullName":"rp_746f6b656e5f7365637265742e53454e54494e454c","modulePath":[],"recursive":false,"decreasing":null,"sourceLifetimeProof":{"schemaVersion":1,"profile":"source-shared-elision-v1","params":[],"outputs":[{"path":[],"kind":"elided","span":{"start":4035909,"end":4035913},"identity":"static"}],"span":{"start":4035893,"end":4035898},"returnOrigins":["static"],"returnLeaves":[{"path":[],"ori